WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.601
the "Tonight Show,"
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.634
You're here.
You're watching the right show.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.901
Thank you.
-Love you, Jimmy!

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.701
-Well -- I love you, too.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.701
Well, guys, one of the biggest
movies of the year,

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:15.167
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"
has finally hit theaters.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.234
Finally.
Fans are going nuts.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.267
People haven't been this pumped
for a Marvel movie

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.100
since the last one
came out a week ago.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.968
Yep, everyone's excited
to see it in theaters.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.968
Even Dr. Fauci was like,
"Screw it.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.734
I got to support this guy."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.901
"He's wearing a mask.
Let's go. I'm ready to go."

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:34.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.567
Yep, as we speak,
fans are lined up

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.267
to see the movie,
including plenty of guys

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.734
dressed like Spider-Man
who definitely can't pull off

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.267
dressing like Spider-Man.
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:45.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.467
In this movie,
Spider-Man has to fight off

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.267
a bunch of crazy villains
at once.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:50.868
And after he does,
he's immediately hired

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.634
as a flight attendant
for United.

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.234
Speaking of airlines,
in a Senate hearing,

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:59.667
the CEOs of Southwest
and American Airlines

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:03.434
both questioned the need
for masks on planes.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.467
Yep, the same thing
actually happened last month

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.868
with the CEO of Spirit
and pants.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:12.133
Yeah, the Southwest CEO was
like, "Who needs masks?

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:15.234
There's plenty of fresh air.
We fly with the top down."

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.834
"Buckle up, everybody!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.801
Speaking of wearing masks
on planes, I heard about

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:22.133
one passenger who tried
work around the rule.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.400
Listen to this.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.734
-A man is now banned from flying
with United Airlines

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:30.300
after deciding to mask up
with a bright red thong.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:37.367
-If you fly Spirit,
that's the oxygen mask

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.234
that drops down in an emergency.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.567
Make sure to put it
on yourself first, then...

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:42.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:46.267
-"Dumps like a truck."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.267
-A few minutes later,
an air marshal walked over

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:49.567
and gave him a mouth wedgie.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.868
It was interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.667
You guys see this?
Former President Trump

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.267
is really upset with his old
chief of staff Mark Meadows

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.234
for writing in his book
that Trump's hair

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:02.367
looked awful when he had COVID.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.067
Must have looked really bad,
because that's how most people

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.968
describe Trump's hair
when he's healthy.

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.934
Meanwhile, I read
that this holiday season,

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:11.801
Melania Trump is releasing
her first NFT,

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.033
called "Melania's Vision,"

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.033
which is a watercolor
of her eyes.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:18.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.501
Donald's like,
"I'm so proud of you.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:21.000
Congrats on the 'nuft.'"

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.334
Yep, Trump's excited about it.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.701
He thinks NFT stands
for "not filing taxes."

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:33.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.667
The cool thing
about Melania's NFT,

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.167
just like she does
with her husband,

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.000
as soon as you turn away,
the eyes roll.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.767
[ Laughter ]
It's amazing.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.200
Hey, this is cool.
In a recent interview,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.601
Usain Bolt said
that playing "Mario Kart"

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:46.901
helped him become
an Olympic champion.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.601
[ Cheers ]
I'm in shock.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.267
'Cause apparently I've been
training for the Olympics

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:53.601
for the last 35 years.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:56.601
Well, get this.
Here in New York, an MTA manager

00:02:56.601 --> 00:03:00.100
was caught with the blow-up doll
in the front seat of his car,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.701
and he's insisting that
he uses it for the company

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.133
and not so that he can drive
in the carpool lane.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:06.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.534
In a related story, he's lying.

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:09.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.601
Guy was like, "Look,
if you have a problem with this,

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.534
talk to my lawyer," and then,
he blew up another doll.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:18.434
And, finally, guys, "Sing 2"
is coming out next week.

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.667
I mean,
we are excited about this.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.200
It has such an amazing cast,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.934
and we wanted to do something
fun with the actors.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:27.067
So we gave them a bunch
of weird phrases

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:30.033
and asked them to sneak those
phrases into their interviews

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.834
as casually as possible.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.767
No one knew we were doing this.
So check it out.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.133
It's time for "Drop It In."

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.133
-♪ Drop It In, Drop It In ♪

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:41.033
♪ D-D-D-D-Drop It In, yeah ♪

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:44.367
-Obviously, everyone's going
to watch "Sing 2" for Christmas.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:45.534
How do you guys plan on

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.634
celebrating Christmas
this year?

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:50.567
-I'm just going to eat
a lot of food, I feel like,

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.868
'cause, you know,
you know what they say --

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:55.400
if you can't lick the spoon,
just eat the bowl, you know?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.634
-That's right.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:59.300
-Which of the following
is not a marsupial --

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.167
kangaroo, koala, or platypus?

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.968
-Koala.
-Platypus have no pouches.

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:08.667
They're the only
egg-laying mammal.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:13.701
-Pouches, eggs,
grape nuts, go nuts.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.667
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:16.667
Yeah.

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:19.033
-I think it's also a movie
about --

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:23.868
about overcoming your own
personal obstacles and --

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:27.133
I mean, even the Pringles Guy
gets lonely in January.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.367
-How many "Sing" stories
do you want to tell?

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.801
Like, have you thought
of what you would write

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:32.968
for "Sing 3" or "Sing 4"?
-There could be a "Sing 3,"

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:37.434
"Sing 4," "Sing 5," "Sing 6,"
"Sing 7," "Sing 8" --

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.968
"Sing 8," yeah -- "Sing 9,"
"Sing 10," "Sing 11,"

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.601
-It'd be like the KIDZ BOP
version of movies!

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:44.501
-..."Sing 12." Yeah! I mean,
you'd skip 13 because of,

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.634
you know, bad vibes.
-Yeah, no, you can never...

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:48.000
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.067
-But, no, I think, otherwise,
it could go on forever.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:53.701
-So, this was obviously,
like, filming during the pand--

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.634
Did you guys get to get together
at any point?

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:59.334
-Oh!
They're g-r-r-rape!

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.501
As T the Tiger says.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.701
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.033
They're g-r-rape!

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.767
-That's sort of the fun
of show business.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.234
And the hard part is, you know,

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:10.367
you get ready, and then there's
someone who can tell you no,

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:13.534
and it's deflating, you know?

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:16.000
It's never a great idea
to microwave a balloon.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.601
[ Ding ]
...and I think that the beauty

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:19.934
of this cast of characters is,
they don't stop.

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.834
-In the film, Buster Moon has
to tell a little white lie.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:25.534
I'm curious to know
if you've ever had to exaggerate

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.167
a special skill to either land
a role or get ahead.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:31.400
-I never will tell a white lie.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.267
And that's something I learned
when I once

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.467
put a balloon
inside of a microwave,

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:39.801
and it's never a good idea to
put a balloon in a microwave.

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:41.567
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.734
I just have
one last thing to say.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:47.300
Nunca es un buen idea poner
un globo en el microondo.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.734
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:52.100
And that's something that is
really important to remember.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.267
-[ Laughs ] Thank you
for sharing that tip with us.

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.167
-Guys, we have exactly
two shows left

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.534
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.601
for that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:03.467
It's time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters."

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:04.667
Here we go.

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:07.067
-♪ "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters" ♪

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:10.701
♪ Two days left ♪

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:11.767
-That's right.

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:14.400
Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.701
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:06:16.701 --> 00:06:19.267
an absurdly cool
Christmas sweater from the

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:21.167
Countdown to
Christmas Cabinet.

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:24.868
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:27.868
...since there are
two shows left,

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:31.234
let's open door number 2.

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:32.467
Where is door number 2?

00:06:32.467 --> 00:06:34.300
Wow!
[ Drum roll ]

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.300
Whenever you're ready.

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:38.133
Yeah! It's Santa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.634
♪♪
Look at that.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:43.467
Whoa! That's a lot of
sweater right there.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:45.434
Oh, it's gorgeous.

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:47.300
Look at that.
Can you turn it around?

00:06:48.868 --> 00:06:53.868
Oh, look at that. Come on.
That's high quality right there.

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:56.200
Now let's see who's gonna go
home with tonight's sweater.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.868
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:06:57.868 --> 00:07:00.234
And if I call your number,
come on down.

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:02.367
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:04.167
Who wants this sweater?
It's a good one.

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:07.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:09.868
232!

00:07:09.868 --> 00:07:11.267
♪♪

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:13.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come on down.

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:20.400
♪♪

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.501
Well, hello!
-Hi.

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:24.400
-Welcome. What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.367
-Abby Lane, from
Nashville, Tennessee.

00:07:26.367 --> 00:07:28.767
-Yeah!
From Nashville, Tennessee.

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:30.834
We love Nashville.

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:31.968
Well, sometimes, it gets cool,

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.501
it gets cozy up there
in Nashville.

00:07:33.501 --> 00:07:34.968
-Sure.

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:36.534
-Would you like to try
this on for the audience...

00:07:36.534 --> 00:07:37.868
-I absolutely would.

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:39.767
-...just so everyone can see
how beautiful it looks.

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:40.868
I think this perfect.

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:43.100
♪♪

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.334
No one will have
this in Nashville.

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:46.567
-No.
-No, no, no.

00:07:46.567 --> 00:07:49.300
Probably any state you go to,
they won't have it.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.667
Tenness-- Oh!
Oh, wow. Look at it.

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:53.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:56.934
That is fant-- Look at that.
You look gorgeous.

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.834
Oh, oh, my -- Yes!
Oh, my goodness.

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:01.234
Fantastic! Thank you so much.

00:08:01.234 --> 00:08:03.801
Congrats to our winner.

